+The local background-safety build supports `AGENT_BROWSER_BACKGROUND=1` for CDP connections. It creates tabs in the background and refuses foreground activation, new windows, and browser-wide shutdown. Tab selection changes only the automation session. Close and idle shutdown close only hidden tabs with persisted proof of creation in the same browser instance. Existing bindings do not prove ownership. Visible agent tabs stay open. Console, error, and network caches have byte budgets. Network output marks incomplete captures, and flow save rejects incomplete captures.
